{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/115428-fiddling-with-changeling","id":115428,"title":"fiddling with changeling","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-18T11:48:14-07:00","id":115428,"title":"fiddling with changeling","content":"For a while i been running a gane of MtA. And i been curious sbout changlings un general. How would s crossover work. Whats their visi\u00f3n on TVE different traditions other than TVE technocracy","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-18T12:14:22-07:00","id":115450,"title":"","content":"I have no idea what TVE means, so I'm not sure I can answer that one.<br /> <br /> As for how crossovers work, that depends. When I'm using another supernatural type as an NPC in a game that's primarily something else, I use the names of the factions/splat from the guest supernatural type. I then run them mainly with the rules found in the back of the main supernatural type's rule book. If there are any powers or abilities that are iconic to the particular guest supernatural, I'll just run it as it and not worry too much about the rules. That way, you don't have to worry about all of the game line specific sub systems for a character that's only in a few sessions.<br /> <br /> In the case of a Changeling NPC in a Mage game, I'd use the Changeling terms like the kith names, the court names, banality, and glamour, but I would use the rules presented for them in the back of the Mage core book. I wouldn't worry about tracking banality. I would just treat the changeling's magic as being more susceptible to paradox. If the NPC is a Pooka, it can change forms when no one is looking. Likewise, a Redcap would get an intimidation bonus, and so forth. That way, it feels like you've got a Changeling in the Mages' midsts, but you as the ST doesn't have to worry about new rules to learn.<br /> <br /> If it's a crossover with multiple PCs of different supernatural types, that's an entirely different situation. What I usually do is make sure I'm familiar with all of the core books involved and decide which game line is dominate in that particular chronicle. That way, if there's metaphysical conflict or a spirit of the game conflict, I know which perspective wins out. Aside from that, each player runs their character's supernatural rules according their particular rule book. If a power relies on a trait another PC doesn't have (such as banality or rage), it's usually easy enough to make up a value that would be appropriate for the character on the fly (a vampire is probably going to have high banality, a mage is probably going to have low rage). Mostly though, the rules are surprisingly compatible despite the game lines' metaphysical incompatibilities. For rules conflicts that aren't addressed by any of the above, everyone has to agree going into it that the ST will be the arbiter in those situations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-18T19:52:14-07:00","id":115665,"title":"","content":"Found this a while back. it has some excellent food for thought in understanding both worlds and how they can overlap.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.moreplans.com/Leah/RPG/crossover.html\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.moreplans.com/Leah/RPG/crossover.html\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.moreplans.com/Leah/RPG/crossover.html\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.moreplans.com/Leah/RPG/crossover.html </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-19T10:50:24-07:00","id":115948,"title":"","content":"TVE was a typo, stupid cellphone. i meant MtA.<br /> <br /> i had in mind a campaing based on The Childrens crusade by neil gaiman. in which hundreds of childrens were kidnap and taken to this &quot;Magic Land.&quot; in which a &quot;Brown Rabbit.&quot; made all their wishes come truth. the catch, the rabbit is a mage exploring the potential of glamour to make himself inmortal, living of their desires and slowly make the childrens die and become toys on the kingdom he runs. so the changelings would find this as a violation and rape of the dreaming itself, sending some changelings to face this being, but also having mages (my players) sinking in this world and trying to find out whats going on","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T14:55:17-07:00","id":122006,"title":"","content":"Crowley I love this storyline. Mind if I snatch it up for a future tabletop game? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>May you live in interesting times...</i><br /> <br /> Storyteller of <b><a href=\"https://sunforgedoath.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Sun Forged Oath</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1998-keichiokami","name":"Keichiokami","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1998_4.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-29T19:58:42-07:00","id":122158,"title":"","content":"sure :P as i said before, i got all the influence from Neil Gaimans &quot;The Children's Crusade.&quot; a graphic novel of the DC vertigo line.<br /> The main rule is that once the mages go in the Childrens Land, they become kids as well, their foci has to be related to childrens toys and games<br /> For example To use<br /> Correponse they would have to play a game related to that (hide and seek or to draw his cross looking game with chalk on the ground)<br /> Life they would use buggers and kisses in case of wounds (you know, when you got an injury and yer mom kissed ya to ease the pain, or bandaids)<br /> Entropy would work through this papper game in which you same someones name, you open it after a certain numer of counts and you find an answer.<br /> Mind: Cooties :P!!!<br /> Spirit: Imaginary friends or halloween costumes.<br /> Time: childrens dont percieve time as the rest of the adults so, this sphere would be sort of useless in the Child Lands.<br /> Cardinal: Orange Juice, Coca Cola and candy.<br /> Matter: Sand (sand Castles) , chalk , toys and childrens science kits<br /> Forces: Waterguns and looking glass + the power of the sun :P<br /> <br /> The paradox would affect if the childrens act like adults,, start to use terms as responsability and such. the players are forced to act as chikldrtens but yet be aware of the situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-30T01:35:05-07:00","id":122243,"title":"","content":"For crossover you can happily use rules as written, changeling the dreaming actually had some of the cleanest crossover rules and most of the time you won't find any thematically aligned conflict anyway. Changelings exist on the stuff of dreams and wonderment of humankind and are harmed by the disbelief of wonder, regimented routines that hold no surprises or freedom for spirit or mind and those who simply embrace a banal humdrum existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-01T23:40:49-07:00","id":123626,"title":"","content":"if you want your mages to take changelings seriously, ignore the idea that they are just little kids in permanant holloween costumes. think of them more as living stories. prior to becomeing changelings they have no concept of reality outside the parameters of their story. once they undergo changelingway they suddenly have those pesky human things like emotions and the ability to change. imagine if you will Snow white, her entire existance is her mother dies and her father marries a woman who tries to kill her, she runs away and meets here seven dwarves eats an apple falls into a coma and gets woke up by prince charming. thats it end of story. nothing more nothing less. she dosn't understand that there is life outside of this set of events and characters and is more or less content to have this be end all of her existance. now suddenly she hops into the body of a teenage girl. she now has a real beating heart and head full of REAL emotions and very real physical flaws. Now imagine she meets prince charming and all is well because its safe and familar but then she meets a cute guy from school who is most certainly NOT apart of her original tale, she suddenly starts to grow and change and become something...more. But she still has access to all the magic and strange dangers that are native to a world that should be impossible.<br /> <br /> I actually ran a changeling game where their magic was more based on Mage than the dreaming where their magic is based off Talecrafting rather than oaths and their rotes are the common abilities called tropes. For example the big bad wolf would Have a Nature and Stage effect for his Huff and puff. (yes i ripped them off the old Realms)<br /> Stage-Corespondence and spirit<br /> Script- anything dealing with character actions and happenstance sort of like entropy and time but not quite<br /> Actor-anything to do with humans life mind and transformations the higher rank the less the character has to be familar with the changeling<br /> Nature- any natural unrefined material or element and animal an plant life<br /> prop-any man made object<br /> fae-anything fae, other changelings, fae creatures also can function as their prime sphere<br /> <br /> paradox might work different for them but i actually ran a changeling game like this and my players loved it. (they all based their characters on video games like Scorpian from Mortal Kombat and Master Chief) the Dreaming Kiths don't necessarily translate well. But the Lost seemings and kiths work great.<br /> <br /> I get that its easier to just use the precreatted setting and crossover rules but i found players have a better time tacking them seriously and have more fun than &quot;hey look its the cuddly wuddly super weak changelings whose magic is all make belief...how cute...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2708-lost_in_the_hedge777","name":"Lost_in_the_Hedge777","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T05:05:04-07:00","id":123723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lost_in_the_Hedge777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/115428-fiddling-with-changeling?p=123626#post123626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get that its easier to just use the precreatted setting and crossover rules but i found players have a better time tacking them seriously and have more fun than &quot;hey look its the cuddly wuddly super weak changelings whose magic is all make belief...how cute...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I had players who thought like this, up until their Vampire character lost an arm, along with the gun he was holding, to a hungry and pissed off Redcap. Changeling magic system has it's flaws but if something it is not weak. It basically has Majesty (VtM Presence 5) power as a level 3 Cantrip. Also I don't know a single person who would call them cuddly, apart from the occasional Pooka who tend to use this kinda thinking to their advantage. My Unseelie Boa Pooka is one of the darkest characters I have played, being sadistic bastard that he was. Also worth considering is if the fact that human disbelief is harmful to Chagneling Magic makes it &quot;make belief&quot; then same is true of Mage Magic as that is just as vulnerable to human belief.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T07:21:47-07:00","id":123767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lost_in_the_Hedge777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/115428-fiddling-with-changeling?p=123626#post123626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;hey look its the cuddly wuddly super weak changelings whose magic is all make belief...how cute...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, you know, you could use <b>actual</b> Changeling: The Dreaming instead whatever it is that's in your head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-02T17:20:09-07:00","id":124139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lost_in_the_Hedge777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/115428-fiddling-with-changeling?p=123626#post123626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if you want your mages to take changelings seriously, ignore the idea that they are just little kids in permanant holloween costumes. think of them more as living stories. prior to becomeing changelings they have no concept of reality outside the parameters of their story. once they undergo changelingway they suddenly have those pesky human things like emotions and the ability to change.<br /> <br /> <br /> I get that its easier to just use the precreatted setting and crossover rules but i found players have a better time tacking them seriously and have more fun than &quot;hey look its the cuddly wuddly super weak changelings whose magic is all make belief...how cute...&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyone who says this is what the Changeling: the Dreaming game is about haven't really given the books much more than a flip through. Anyone thinking that's what changeling is about shouldn't be running a changeling game.<br /> <br /> I do find your take on the changeling magic system making it more like mage is very interesting. I do feel that the changeling Magic system is hobbled by a lot of flaws and really should be more flexible like Mage. In my games I impress upon my mage players that they should think of a Changeling like a Marauder that you can't find or see coming and can hardly defend yourself against. Especially if they like you and want to be your friend. Throw in the fact there can be a whole lot of them and as soon as you mess with one, a whole sh**storm of madness can come your way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-06T20:21:47-07:00","id":127202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lost_in_the_Hedge777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/115428-fiddling-with-changeling?p=123626#post123626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">if you want your mages to take changelings seriously, ignore the idea that they are just little kids in permanant holloween costumes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that the latter is a gross misrepresentation of the themes and mood of CtD, I agree whole-heartedly. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lost_in_the_Hedge777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/115428-fiddling-with-changeling?p=123626#post123626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">think of them more as living stories. prior to becomeing changelings they have no concept of reality outside the parameters of their story. once they undergo changelingway they suddenly have those pesky human things like emotions and the ability to change. imagine if you will Snow white, her entire existance is her mother dies and her father marries a woman who tries to kill her, she runs away and meets here seven dwarves eats an apple falls into a coma and gets woke up by prince charming. thats it end of story. nothing more nothing less. she dosn't understand that there is life outside of this set of events and characters and is more or less content to have this be end all of her existance. now suddenly she hops into the body of a teenage girl. she now has a real beating heart and head full of REAL emotions and very real physical flaws. Now imagine she meets prince charming and all is well because its safe and familar but then she meets a cute guy from school who is most certainly NOT a part of her original tale, she suddenly starts to grow and change and become something...more. But she still has access to all the magic and strange dangers that are native to a world that should be impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds like it could be a fun CtL game, with Charlatans as the protagonists. But it bears about as much resemblance to CtD as the derogatory remark above does. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lost_in_the_Hedge777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/115428-fiddling-with-changeling?p=123626#post123626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually ran a changeling game where their magic was more based on Mage than the dreaming where their magic is based off Talecrafting rather than oaths and their rotes are the common abilities called tropes. For example the big bad wolf would Have a Nature and Stage effect for his Huff and puff. (yes i ripped them off the old Realms)</div> </div> </div> </div>Hush; you wouldn\u2019t want anyone to get the mistaken impression that you were actually using something from CtD in a nominally CtD game\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lost_in_the_Hedge777</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/115428-fiddling-with-changeling?p=123626#post123626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stage-Corespondence and spirit<br /> Script- anything dealing with character actions and happenstance sort of like entropy and time but not quite<br /> Actor-anything to do with humans life mind and transformations the higher rank the less the character has to be familar with the changeling<br /> Nature- any natural unrefined material or element and animal an plant life<br /> prop-any man made object<br /> fae-anything fae, other changelings, fae creatures also can function as their prime sphere<br /> <br /> paradox might work different for them but i actually ran a changeling game like this and my players loved it. (they all based their characters on video games like Scorpian from Mortal Kombat and Master Chief) the Dreaming Kiths don't necessarily translate well. But the Lost seemings and kiths work great.</div> </div> </div> </div>I certainly wouldn\u2019t mind a more flexible variation of CtD\u2019s magic system. But I\u2019d rather not do it by tossing the Arts out the window. CtD\u2019s Arts-and-Realms system has tremendous potential for flexibility; and I\u2019d rather see that played up, perhaps with an adaptation of DAFae\u2019s Unleashing Dominions mechanic to go alongside the standard Cantrips system that CtD already has. <br /> <br /> I could see the Unleashing of a Realm being something similar in feel to CtD2e\u2019s Calling Upon the Wyrd: it manifests the power of the Dreaming directly in the mortal world for all to see, with all the consequences that go along with that. I\u2019d also invert the usual relationship between Arts and Realms: where each Art defines a set of Cantrips that are tailored in their specific effects by your choice of Realms, each Realm would have a series of Unleashings with capabilities that span the Arts; and knowledge of a particular Art would let you Unleash the Realms in ways related to it with less danger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T23:16:48-07:00","id":128022,"title":"","content":"okay i'll admit i'm more biased towards the lost than i am the dreaming: the name should have given it away. i like the versatility in character creation better and the fact the their powers are actually &quot;real&quot; ( or as real as role playing game powers can be.) <br /> <br /> and yes i'll admit that my choice of words was poor one. i have read changeling the dreaming and despite appearances i enjoy the idea of it, sadly that's the reaction i get from most players (and that's being nice about it). but i also have issues with the setting myself.<br /> <br /> a big problem i have with the dreaming is in fact, banality. if someone doesn't believe in faeries, their powers and pretty much everything that makes them Fae falters against the crushing weight of modern cynicism if not fails outright. yes mages have the same problem but at least their abilities have some bite to it and no I'm not opening up to redcap jokes here. <br /> <br /> I can get into the idea of a game where faery tales are real and things like true loves kiss, dastardly curses and wishing upon a star is literal reality. i can get into the idea that wonder and romance are alive in the world of darkness and fae nature stuggles to co-exist with the realities of the human world. <br /> <br /> what i have a problem with is that they struggle to exist at all in the world of darkness. yes i get it that's a theme that permeates the whole setting. but it doesn't mean you have to make the Fae look like chumps next to the garou or the kindred just because they happen to be moodier and more cynical. look at Fables, they were less concerned about people believing in them and more concerned with the consequences of whether or not the mundy world would wipe them out if discovered and they were still BAD ASS about it. which i'm sure is possible with the dreaming sadly, i have never been able to play in a game like that nor convince anyone to let me run one. <br /> <br /> <br /> sorry if i came off as rather snariling but changeling the dreaming has been one of the really great frustrations of my gaming life. i'd LOVE to play an actual changeling game where what people enjoy about it but at this point i doubt it'll ever happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2708-lost_in_the_hedge777","name":"Lost_in_the_Hedge777","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2708_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T03:55:58-07:00","id":128125,"title":"","content":"I completely agree with you about the flaws in the system for Dreaming. While I can see Banality as having it's place as a consequence, sort of (but not exactly like) Paradox is for the Mage game; (In my mind it should be more like Gauntlet difficulties) however the system is not well balanced in that respect. The power base while dynamic and rich with possibilities for creative players and STs is unfairly weak in its ratings and cost. Like a vampire who's constantly internally bleeding on top of their thirst for blood. In that drive to feed sense, Changelings can be terrifying. No amount of Glamour is ever enough and if they get their hands on a Mage and convince them to forget Reality and consequences and party with them, well, you have the makings of a Quiet and all the Changeling has to do is shake hands with the Mage. But still, the system has some major flaws in execution even if the premiss is sound, and I have pointed out some of these flaws in another thread and a rantier post. We understand and agree with you on this much. It's not as powerful, or flexible as a magic system for Changeling could be that would put them more on the level of Formori or Marauders in terms of &quot;things you don't want to mess with&quot; in the World of Darkness. Have a look at Dark Ages: Fae and you'll see a big difference in magic styles that was probably more what you're expecting from Changeling Dreaming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T04:09:40-07:00","id":128134,"title":"","content":"In case you wanna have a look Hedge, I highly recommend the discussions on these threads in regards to flaws that bug fans about Changeling D and comparisons between DA:Fae and Changeling Lost. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/53897-dark-ages-fae\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/53897-dark-ages-fae\"> Dark Ages: Fae - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/53897-dark-ages-fae\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/53897-dark-ages-fae </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I just read this book and after years and years of hating ANYTHING C:TD related (sorry, it just doesn't appeal to me) I have to say.... WOW. I really like what they did with it and how it evolved. I'm pretty sure that if C:TD had been like DA:F I would have really gotten into it all those years ago. </div> </div> </div> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/79695-my-probelm-with-changeling\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/79695-my-probelm-with-changeling\"> My Probelm with Changeling - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/79695-my-probelm-with-changeling\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/79695-my-probelm-with-changeling </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I know that there's a C20 thread right now that's gone off tangent a bit towards this, but I felt that I'd rather start a new thread instead of risking derailing that one further. With M20 around the corner and Wr20 in the works, to some extent talk of C20 is a bit early. However, as has been noted </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-08T11:18:57-07:00","id":128383,"title":"","content":"I've never seen that many flaws with the Arts and Realms system and Changelings have never felt weak to me when compared next to the other supernaturals. Banality is often misunderstood and Autumn People is a good guidebook about it. Simply not believing in magic doesn't make someone &quot;Banal&quot; that makes them an average Mortal (Banality 6-7) now sure, this means if you're trying to effect said mortal with Arts things are tricky to do in a couple of seconds. However give it a minute and it becomes a lot easier through the use of Bunks or throw some Glamour at the situation. Faeries have some rediculous magic at their disposal, but it's not always quick to do. As to Realms? I've always liked them. Faerie tales and myth lore are full of the restrictions on the actions of the Fae as well as the warnings of what they will do. All it takes is some creative thinking to get some solid use out of them and a few experience points down the line the restrictions tend to slip away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T04:08:48-07:00","id":128861,"title":"","content":"But if you're a grump and your Glamour pool is low, you can't throw much Glamour around in combat. It's like you have to max out your character before you can be any kind of effective with magic. For beings supposedly purely magical, that seems like a big flaw right there. I cited a good example in the above posted Dark Ages Thread. Care to explain how things like that do not constitute flaws in the system, Moirdryd?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T10:25:26-07:00","id":129074,"title":"","content":"The Glamour economy is one of the bigger problems with Changeling rules as written. Aside from that, if you assume changelings regain Glamour at a reasonable rate, Grumps can't use their faerie magic as freely as a Childling, but it's not crippling. They can still get at least one scene per session where they get to cut loose and be a powerful faerie. For one Glamour and one Willpower point, they can Call Upon the Wyrd. This makes their faerie mien, any chimerical companions they may have, and all of their magic Wyrd for one scene, so they no longer have to spend any Glamour for the rest of the scene. Once the low Glamour pool has been bypassed, as others have pointed out, overcoming most Banality ratings are fairly trivial. That only becomes problematic when you're dealing with a Dauntain or a full on Autumn Person, and any changeling is going to have issues with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-09T18:05:10-07:00","id":129455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PookaKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/115428-fiddling-with-changeling?p=129074#post129074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Glamour economy is one of the bigger problems with Changeling rules as written. Aside from that, if you assume changelings regain Glamour at a reasonable rate, Grumps can't use their faerie magic as freely as a Childling, but it's not crippling. They can still get at least one scene per session where they get to cut loose and be a powerful faerie. For one Glamour and one Willpower point, they can Call Upon the Wyrd. This makes their faerie mien, any chimerical companions they may have, and all of their magic Wyrd for one scene, so they no longer have to spend any Glamour for the rest of the scene. Once the low Glamour pool has been bypassed, as others have pointed out, overcoming most Banality ratings are fairly trivial. That only becomes problematic when you're dealing with a Dauntain or a full on Autumn Person, and any changeling is going to have issues with that.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. But if say you're starting out with a Perm Glamour rating of 3, no matter the Childling or Grump, that doesn't give you much to use even if you Wyrd in combat. And if you don't have chimerical companions because you're still starting out, then you're that much more vulnerable. Having chimerical companions sure helps, but then you have to rely on having an imaginary army with you every time you have a confrontation. Add to that the necessity to have Fae 5 rating just to fight ANYthing supernatural including your own kind, and the restrictions start to get ridiculous. Not that Changeling is supposed to be all hack n slash, but when you're having a campaign even as simple as the Toybox, combat becomes the weakest and most difficult part to get through. Nevermind fighting a Vampire or a Hunter or anything interesting. I've seen games become mired in political court intrigue because it's just easier to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-10T04:33:29-07:00","id":129789,"title":"","content":"There are several ways around the perceived &quot;flaws&quot; and a lot of them have to do with storyteller theme as much as raw (as a large amount of RAW relies on Storyteller influence for Changeling)<br /> I've always seen this as a deliberate attempt to help Changeling Chronicles work in certain ways.<br /> <br /> Here are a few of the available methods to doing magical stuff<br /> <br /> 1) Just like in Mage where I think 99% of characters out of chargen spend to raise Arete to 2, so it's only 6 freebies to add +2 to your Glamour, that's a Grump with Glamour 5, Wilder with 6 or Childling with 7.<br /> <br /> 2) Enchanting the target of your desires makes things easier and less glamour intensive (although sometimes tricky to achieve in the first place) <br /> <br /> 3) Think of realms as mini Paradigms (since we are in a MTA-CTD crossover topic) it's all about what you can get away with in a Story (namely Your personal faerie tale). Play cleverly and you don't need a high Actor realm to effect mortal and non-dreaming super-naturals. Also if you can get an additional Realm on the target you can drop difficulties by 1<br /> <br /> 4) Bunks! These things are important and handle similar to stunts in Exalted/Scion for the conceptualisation along with Rotes etc in Mage. A simple bunk (level 1) drops the diff by 1 so you should always use them as it doesn't require a dice action. You can, by splitting your Dice pool, get a Level 2 Bunk off in the casting turn itself (so -2 difficulty for half the dice). Given a round or two's prep time life gets easier. <br /> <br /> 5) Perhaps most importantly, Dross. This is so often overlooked and yet it's a major component in Changeling society and the game. It's even used as part of currency amongst the fair ones. The Dross section in chapter 7 covers a lot of possibilities but people only remember the big ones. Need an extra Glamour boost? Well that Graffiti Mural on the wall next to you may well contain a point of glimmering Glamour. Just used a load of Glamour in a fight with the Corby? Go hunting and consume Chimerical flesh to regain Glamour, the same if you've just slain the Manticore, feast and replenish as in the good old tales of heroes. Be inventive, ask the questions of the ST, Changeling is about finding the lingering magic of the Dream in the world. Often in crossover some supernaturals themselves may provide Dross (Vampire blood for example). This is what the Kenning Talent is Really Really handy for. <br /> <br /> 6) Reverie and Ravaging: (Also Dreamers Background) The former is quicker and easier than the latter but it's worth understanding how Both work. Odds are if you have a dreamer or know an npc who you're trying to guide to reverie that they may well be making dross too! (Some online games even implemented systems around this to give people an even standard) and any fae can turn Unseelie for a while and rip the dreams of mortals from their conciousness. The Musing and Ravaging Thresholds are again a roleplaying tool. Use them inventively.<br /> <br /> 7) Treasures: A very handy background often looked at in Weird and Wonderful ways but some clever tricks are overlooked. Say an ancient tome of faerie magic that grants bonuses to Realms while it's being used or a wand that lowers a cantrip difficulty for a certain Art and so forth. <br /> <br /> 8) Remember! When calculating Cantrip Difficulty it maxes out at 10 before you start deducting for Glamour, Bunks, Additional realms etc. So Joe Human with a banality of 7 (cantrip diff banality +4) Calculates down from 10 NOT 11. <br /> <br /> <br /> Now I've said all that if people really feel the fae are lacking and want to play with the system there are some very easy ways to do this<br /> <br /> 1) Realms: All Realms begin at 1 dot and then you get your 5 to spend. <br /> 2) Glamour: Raise all starting Glamour's by 1, reduce the Freebie points cost to 2. <br /> 3) Cantrip Difficulty: Reduce to Banality +3<br /> 4) Drop the +1 Difficulty for Modifier (Time and Scene realms). This is a house rule that I use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T00:00:30-07:00","id":131747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darling_Rose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/115428-fiddling-with-changeling?p=129455#post129455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Add to that the necessity to have Fae 5 rating just to fight ANYthing supernatural including your own kind, and the restrictions start to get ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fae one is sufficient if fighting Commoner Kithain, Fae 2 for Noble Kithain (Sidhe+any commoners with a Title), Fae 3 for any Chimerae and 4 for ALL other Fae beings or anything else related to the Dreaming. Level 5 is ONLY needed to affect Glamour directly, that is casting effects on Dross or Countering Cantrips or just manipulating raw Glamour in some way. So basically fighting other kithains 1-2 is quite enough but if facing other Fae beings with regularity then you may have use for Fae up to 4 and level five is mostly reserved for Sorcerers.<br /> <br /> Other supernaturals are covered by Actor which does have it's problems in execution. Basically 2-3 should be enough unless you already are in dire enmity with the being, which of course raises the question that if he becomes an enemy through your cantrip do further castings suddenly require Actor 5 which seems to be the case by RAW.<br /> <br /> Besides one can nicely move around these restrictions through creative use of Prop realm which does govern amongst other things the clothes and weapons of your enemy which should give you a load of possibilities even with just low amounts of the Realm.<br /> <br /> The biggest problem with CtD is still Glamour economy since almost everything, even Birthrights, cost Glamour and you have a very limited pool of it that is extremely slow to refill normally. I generally as a house-rule tend to eliminate Glamour costs from Birthrights as a minor fix although I have been planning a more throughout revision of Glamour but that is for another time. Still while that is the main issue the Realms have some fixing to do as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T02:29:32-07:00","id":131943,"title":"","content":"Actually Possessed, you only need the high levels of Actor if you know nothing about your target (4) or you know nothing and they're your enemy (5), make them talk with you (mid fight conversation scene), learn their name and all you need is 2-3. So, odds are if 2-3 was sufficient before it will still be so, it's why learning someone's name has so much power. Glamour Economy I've never found to be an issue, but again Dross has always been the way around as has being careful with what you're casting, of course if regaining Glamour is an issue you can always allow Changelings to regain a point after a night (or day) dreaming, anything more than that and you're making the Dreaming far far more common in the Mortal world and Glamour starts getting spent like Bloodpoints.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T09:59:58-07:00","id":132355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/115428-fiddling-with-changeling?p=131943#post131943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually Possessed, you only need the high levels of Actor if you know nothing about your target (4) or you know nothing and they're your enemy (5)</div> </div> </div> </div> Unfortunately, that's not what the rules actually say. Any non-fae your character is in any fight or competition with puts them in Actor 5 territory. The book even give an example of playing a game with your best friend means you need Actor 5 to affect them during the game. It's dumb, and hopefully something that'll be addressed if there's a C20. My other comments have already been covered by Possesed <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-11T11:39:42-07:00","id":132514,"title":"","content":"Very true Pookaknight, but that aspect of Actor 5 flies in the face of everything else the Realm allows for and how it's described as working towhit &quot;The Higher the realm the less you need to know about your target&quot;, a gaming friend, while there conflicts with the rest of the Realm and I always took that to mean somebody you've never met before whom you are in competition with. At my table and in every game I've ever played in its been interpreted as I originally presented. Of course that's down to an interpretation along with using Level 3 for Familliar Face (RAW) or (and this has been done a lot) merely learning your target's name.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T00:58:57-07:00","id":135095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/115428-fiddling-with-changeling?p=132514#post132514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very true Pookaknight, but that aspect of Actor 5 flies in the face of everything else the Realm allows for and how it's described as working towhit &quot;The Higher the realm the less you need to know about your target&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Changeling Dreaming is chock full of little contradictions like that. That's what makes it a tricky and finicky system to try and work with. Unless you are hacking or making up House rules for it, even if you are using the system loopholes to your advantage, it still has makes for some headaches. Any of the other games you can play a character right out of the box so to speak, even with randomized stats and be Ok. Maybe a bit disadvantaged. But when everyone wanting to have an average and effective Fae character has to carefully use your freebies in character creation to overcome imbalanced limitations that will affect their Glamour pool before they even begin playing... there's something broken with that system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T01:39:57-07:00","id":135111,"title":"","content":"I think we are starting to assess in differant directions Darling Rose. Addressing the &quot;Glamour Limitations&quot; earlier and internal inconsistency of the Actor Realm (which as I mentioned is so easily overlooked as to be ignored without comment) has been mostly done thus far to apply to the CrossOver context of the OP. I've run it myself and played in a lot of crossover games (mostly online) New Bremen, New Bremen's revisited, Midnight Garden, Sierra Dreams, Immortal Vigilence, Puerto Nostra, Hecates Peace, Deadly Games (and it's predessor) and a few others who's names I forget. It all used to work fine with but a few tweaks to clarify points of crossover and the occasional actual issue of two systems colliding. &quot;Out of the box&quot; though, as in playing a game of CTD as CTD it is 100% as playable as any of the other original 5 games, Glamour becomes less an issue because you're interacting with chimera a lot more often, you're also more likely to have access to the Dreaming and you can focus Realms without worry of needing an ST interpretation or house rule for Actor as much because crossover isn't happening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T03:45:13-07:00","id":139158,"title":"","content":"The Actor 5 thing just underlines the necessity of other realms. The unseelie sidhe sends a gang of mortal ruffins armed with pipes to teach you some respect, but you only have actor 1? No problem, because you have prop and scene!<br /> <br /> - Holly Strike their weapons. This cantrip deals some piddly agg damage, which everyone remembers, but it also obliterates pounds and pounds of matter. ANY matter. It melts butter and vaporizes titanium with equal power. A bunch of hoodlums whose weapons explode when you throw birdseed at them and go &quot;two magic, two magic!&quot; is going to reconsider their career choices.Especially if they end up buck naked as part of the deal.<br /> <br /> - Use Dictum on the weapons! It's a little &quot;out there,&quot; but if your ST doesn't let you go &quot;out there&quot; while playing changeling, he's not doing his job. Command the pipes to not hit you. May call for some resisted rolls as the thugs try to force their tools to overcome your dictates, but still pretty effective.<br /> <br /> - Alternately, use Ensnare's second effect to make those pipes hit <i>them</i>.<br /> <br /> - Pyretics 3 makes the pipes catch on fire... not too great if they hit you, but since the pipes are now burning the crap out of the thugs holding them...<br /> <br /> To say nothing of what you can do with the rest of the scenery around them. the weird setting for Actor 5 really just means you have to use other Realms to make reality go bonkers around your enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-16T08:04:01-07:00","id":139336,"title":"","content":"That too... I've seen redcaps bully brow beat security doors open (they can intimidate Anything! after all)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T14:31:37-07:00","id":144863,"title":"","content":"I'd argue that the Banality of any given member of the Society of Ether can be high or low, depending; they are fringe and mad scientists, after all. Nockers can get along swimmingly with many from this Tradition. It's all about how you spin it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://s6.postimg.org/h38q1qmfx/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://s6.postimg.org/67hc6e1i5/i_backed_ex3_small.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2045-melonlord82","name":"melonlord82","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2045_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}